From 9fca2f1b110cbf4fd131994fecb78b78325d7e5b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Guodong Xu <guodong.xu@oss.qualcomm.com>
Date: Sun, 20 Sep 2026 03:18:25 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 027/468] UPSTREAM: riscv: dts: spacemit: k3: Add Zic64b ISA
 extension

The K3 X100 cores have 64-byte cache blocks, already described by their
cbom/cbop/cboz-block-size of 64, so they implement Zic64b, a mandatory
RVA23 extension.  Declare it in each core's riscv,isa-extensions.

Reviewed-by: Yixun Lan <dlan@kernel.org>
Signed-off-by: Guodong Xu <guodong.xu@oss.qualcomm.com>
Link: https://patch.msgid.link/20260920-rva23u64-hwprobe-v2-v8-5-5f14bc5c23d3@oss.qualcomm.com
Signed-off-by: Paul Walmsley <pjw@kernel.org>
(cherry picked from commit 7c4752c60f99be4a9a4c573ba86eacbe5d3cc823)
Signed-off-by: Han Gao <gaohan@iscas.ac.cn>
